        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best carpet cleaner for most homes?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For most homes with wall-to-wall carpet, a heated upright with a large tank and long cord is the best choice, such as the Bissell Revolution HydroSteam Pet. If your budget is tighter, the ProHeat 2X Revolution Pet Pro family offers similar scrubbing for less money. Pair either with a portable for stairs and spills.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is it better to buy or rent a carpet cleaner?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                If you deep-clean carpet more than once a year, or you have pets that cause frequent messes, owning usually costs less than renting over time and lets you treat stains immediately. If you clean once every few years, renting a large machine can make sense. Professional cleaning is best for heavily soiled or warrantied carpet.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long does carpet take to dry after cleaning?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It depends on the carpet, the amount of water used and the room's humidity. Carpet is often dry to the touch in a few hours and fully dry within about a day. Bissell advertises a 30-minute Quick Dry mode on the HydroSteam Pet but notes results vary. Extra dry passes, fans and a dehumidifier shorten drying.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can I use a carpet cleaner on upholstery?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Usually yes, with the hose and an upholstery tool, but check the fabric's care code first. Many upholstered pieces are labeled for water-based cleaning, but some are solvent-only or dry-clean only. Test a hidden area, use as little water as possible and extract thoroughly so the cushion fill does not stay damp.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do carpet cleaners remove pet urine smell?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                They can, if the urine has not soaked deep into the pad. Treat the area with an enzyme cleaner designed for pet urine, let it dwell as directed, then extract slowly with several dry passes. If odor returns after cleaning, the pad underneath may be contaminated and need replacing.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the difference between a carpet cleaner and a steam cleaner?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Most home carpet cleaners are hot-water extractors: they spray warm water and solution and suck it back out. Some, like Bissell's HydroSteam, add a heater to warm the solution. Neither reaches the temperatures of a professional truck-mounted system, and a hard-floor steam mop is a different tool that is not designed for carpet.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How often should I deep-clean my carpet?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Many carpet manufacturers suggest professional or deep cleaning about every 12 to 18 months, more often in homes with pets, kids or heavy traffic. Check your carpet warranty for its specific requirement. Between deep cleans, vacuum regularly and treat spills quickly with a portable spot cleaner.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
